## You Could Have a Lemon Law Case If…

- The manufacturer has made a reasonable number of attempts to repair the warranty-covered defect.

- The vehicle has been out of service for warranty-covered repairs for 30 or more cumulative days.

- The vehicle’s defects were not caused by driver abuse, error, or neglect.

With lemon law cases, the faster you act, the better. You need to report the defects to the manufacturer while your car is still under its original warranty. [Reach out to the team](/contact) at CLINE APC for a free case evaluation. Our experienced, assertive lemon law attorneys in Santa Clarita will review the facts, walk you through your options, and help you fight for the compensation you’re owed.

