## How to File Your Lemon Law Claim

Here’s a step-by-step guide to filing a lemon law claim in Santa Clarita.

- Bring your car to a manufacturer-authorized repair centre for diagnosis and service.

- Keep thorough records of every repair attempt, including:

- A clear summary of the recurring defects or issues.

- The dates of each repair appointment.

- The total number of days your vehicle has been in the shop.

- Copies of all repair invoices, work orders, and receipts.

- Any emails, letters, or messages exchanged with the manufacturer or dealership regarding your car’s defects.

- Consult a competent Santa Clarita lemon law lawyer.

## California Lemon Law and Used Cars

California lemon law can cover pre-owned vehicles, but specific conditions must be met to determine eligibility.

## Dealership Warranty on Pre-Owned Cars

Many California dealerships offer limited warranties on used cars, typically covering the first 30 days or 1,000 miles, whichever comes first. If your vehicle develops a serious defect during this period and meets the legal criteria, you may have grounds for a lemon law claim.

## Consumer Protections for Used Vehicles

Under CA lemon law, dealerships are responsible for covering repair costs, offering a replacement, or issuing a refund if a used vehicle qualifies as a lemon. Additionally, all legal fees are covered by the warrantor.

## “As-Is” Purchases

Purchasing a car “as-is” means you take full responsibility for any issues or defects after the sale. In most cases, as-is vehicles are not covered under California lemon law. Dealerships are required to disclose the as-is status on the buyer’s guide while the car is on display. If this disclosure was missing or misrepresented, you may still have legal options.

